WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.340
- So this Newsmax panel absolutely lost

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.617
their freaking minds when
some high school student said

00:00:04.617 --> 00:00:07.150
"Allah" instead of "God" in
the Pledge of Allegiance.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.890
- One nation, under Allah.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.740
- Let's put aside that "Allah"
is just "God" in Arabic,

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.339
and that, correct me if
I'm wrong, but under Islam,

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:18.830
Allah is explicitly the
same God as the Christian

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.100
and Jewish God, as well,
and let's put aside

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.060
that multiculturalism and
the freedom of religion is

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.520
about as American as it gets,

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.470
but let's focus on the law itself.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:28.110
For 80 years, under the First Amendment,

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.140
you cannot make flag salutes

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.530
and the Pledge of Allegiance compulsory,

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.930
and you can't make high
school students do it,

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.260
especially the way that
you want them to do it.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.790
And perhaps one of the greatest quotes

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.747
from a Supreme Court case ever reads,

00:00:39.747 --> 00:00:40.780
"If there's any fixed star

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.230
in our constitutional constellation,

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.555
it is that no official,
high or petty, can prescribe

00:00:44.555 --> 00:00:47.940
what shall be orthodox in
politics, nationalism, religion,

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.130
or other matters of opinion,

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.760
or for citizens to confess by word

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.660
or act their faith therein."

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.493
I think it's pretty cool if
not exceptionally American

00:00:55.493 --> 00:00:58.110
that this high school student
felt comfortable riffing

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.453
on the Pledge of Allegiance.

